Rust crates in the revue binary
===============================

The revue binary is compiled from revue's own code (MIT License, see LICENSE) and
the Rust crates below, from crates.io. Each crate keeps its own license, given
here from the crate's own license file, or as the license's standard text when
the crate has none. A crate offered under a choice of licenses is listed under
the one used here. The JavaScript libraries in revue's UI are listed in
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.

This one file covers the binaries for every platform, so it may name a few
crates that a given binary doesn't include.

